  "reason": "CDC CBC_H flags RDW/WBC instrument effects; both are used in internally calibrated KDM. Cycle is added to every structural regression while exposures, outcomes, scales, survey design, missingness and spline knots stay fixed. Cycle-specific variants retain the common data scales and use design subpopulations.",
  "interpretation_rules": [
    "Do not replace primary estimates or select variants by P value.",
    "Compare estimates and uncertainty, not only significance categories.",
    "Cycle-specific cognition effects are descriptive because factor measurement invariance is not established.",
    "Between-cycle contrasts are restricted to biological-measure paths and age interactions on a common scale.",
    "Use reported standard errors for independent-cycle contrasts; the cycles use distinct strata/PSUs.",
    "Period adjustment does not identify or correct the actual within-2012 instrument transition; retain this limitation.",
    "No activity-volume-adjusted flexible interactions or nonlinear full-path indirect effects are introduced by this audit."
  ],
  "input_format_fix": "NAMES variables, including CYCLE2, precede DEFINE-created products in USEVARIABLES; model set and hypotheses unchanged."
